      "created_at": "2018-10-27T17:59:25Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-27T17:59:25Z",
      "body": "@randomshell time is not the problem, but I am wary of situations like this where something _seems_ more privacy-safe while in reality it has some hidden caveat.\r\n\r\nIf I interpret these privacy rules incorrectly and there is just Cloudflare/APNIC with access to data then we can add it; if unfortunately there is less data collected but it is shared between Cloudflare and Mozilla, then I vote against adding this. Probably users of Bromite would not select the option since it is equivalent to regular Cloudflare with the added \"benefit\" that another company can use the (anonymised) data for whatever purpose.\r\n\r\nThanks for your interest, we all have to stay vigilant; I still hope there will be some day an EFF-sponsored DoH server but they do not seem much interested in operating services.",
